   "source": [
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, cross_val_score\n",
    "\n",
    "y_data = df[\"selling_price\"]\n",
    "x_data = df.drop([\"selling_price\",\"name\", \"seats\", \"mileage\"], axis=1).astype(\"float64\")\n",
    "\n",
    "x_train, x_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(x_data, y_data, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"number of test samples :\", x_test.shape[0])\n",
    "print(\"number of training samples:\", x_train.shape[0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "71e4843b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.8 Data Standrization"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 127,
   "id": "adc5c1a8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "x_scaled_train = scaler.fit_transform(x_train)\n",
    "x_scaled_train\n",
    "x_scaled_test = scaler.fit_transform(x_test)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9a7ec61e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3 Model Development and Evaluation\n",
    "for this experiment, we will use to type of regression models:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Linear Regression model: Model that finds the best line that fits the linear data so that it finds the linear relationship between the features and the target\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Polynomial Model: Model that finds nonlinear relationship between the independent variable and the target variable which is a curve that fits the data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 128,
   "id": "c7798aa2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "---The R^2 for the Linear Regression model is:  0.8360960743503348 ---\n",
      "---The MSE for the Linear Regression model is:  0.11228761485065665 ---\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "LR_model = LinearRegression()\n",
    "LR_model.fit(x_scaled_train, y_train)\n",
    "print(\"---The R^2 for the Linear Regression model is: \", LR_model.score(x_scaled_test, y_test), \"---\")\n",
    "print(\"---The MSE for the Linear Regression model is: \",mean_squared_error(y_test, LR_model.predict(x_scaled_test)), \"---\")"
   ]
  },
