   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The below graph shows the relationship between the degree of the model and R^2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "17378b9c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "Rsqu_train, Rsqu_test = [], []\n",
    "order = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "for n in order:\n",
    "    pr = PolynomialFeatures(degree=n)\n",
    "    xtr = pr.fit_transform(x_scaled_train)\n",
    "    xte = pr.transform(x_scaled_test)\n",
    "    lr_temp = LinearRegression().fit(xtr, y_train)\n",
    "    Rsqu_train.append(lr_temp.score(xtr, y_train))\n",
    "    Rsqu_test.append(lr_temp.score(xte, y_test))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot(order, Rsqu_train, \"ro-\", label=\"Training data\")\n",
    "plt.plot(order, Rsqu_test, \"bo-\", label=\"Test data\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"order\"); plt.ylabel(\"R^2\"); plt.title(\"R^2 vs polynomial order\"); plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b5b8d685",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "As shown in the above graph, the R^2 has been increased from orders 1-3 in both training and test process, but it starts to decrease from 4 to 6 orders. the training data continued to increase to the 4th order but the test score is less in this degree which means that the model overfits the data in this interval."
   ]
